  <content>
  <section><title>Adding Systems of Equations and Using Their Graphs</title>
<para>Look at the system of equations shown here:</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}&amp;&amp;\left\{\begin{array}{l}–3x\;+\;4y\;=\;7\\3x\;+\;2y\;=\;17\end{array}\right.\end{array}\)</para>
<para>Let’s graph each equation on the coordinate plane. Identify the point of intersection.</para>
<figure><media alt="GRAPH OF TWO LINES INTERSECTING AT THE POINT (3, 4)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5f191fe3bedabe49601739750eeed7490efb4923"/></media></figure><emphasis/>
<para>The lines intersect at \((3, 4)\).</para>
<para>Add the two equations together. Simplify the resulting equation.</para>
<para>\(\begin{array}{r}-3x+4y=7\\3x+2y=17\\\hline6y=24\\y=4\end{array}\) </para>
<para>Graph the resulting equation on the same coordinate plane.</para>
<figure><media alt="GRAPH OF THREE LINES INTERSECTING AT THE POINT (3,4)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0dce7e1312aff88580115970deb60e42d6fcfc3a"/></media></figure><emphasis/>
<para>All three lines intersect at \((3, 4)\). </para>
<para>You verified that by adding the two equations in the system, you created a third equation that is also true.</para>
<para>The solution to the system is \(x = 3\), \(y = 4\).</para>
<title>Try It: Adding Systems of Equations and Using Their Graphs</title>
<para>Add the equations to find the resulting equation. Then graph all three equations to find the ordered pair where they intersect.</para>
<para>Use this system of equations to answer questions 1 – 4.</para>
<para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{c}-2x-3y=7\\2x+y=3\end{array}\right.\)</para>


<!--Q#1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Add the equations to find the resulting equation. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(\underline{\;\;\;\;\;-2x-3y=7\\+\;\;\;\;\;\;\;2x+y=3}\\\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;-2y\;=10\\\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;y\;=-5\\\) </para>
    
    <para> \(9\begin{array}{rcl}2x+\;y&amp;=&amp;3\;\\2x+\;(-5)&amp;=&amp;3\\2x&amp;=&amp;8\\x&amp;=&amp;4\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


